explanation:
You come first; then Bheeshma, Karna,
Kripa, great warriors; Ashwaththama,
Vikarna, and the son of Somadhatta;

translation:
In that peace, all pains are destroyed;
for the intellect of the tranquil-minded
soon becomes steady.

Whatever a great man does, others also do;
whatever he establishes as the standard,
the world follows.

The worshippers of the gods go to them;
the ancestor-worshippers go to the manes;
the worshippers of the deities who preside
over the elements go to them; but My

Better indeed is knowledge than practice;
better than knowledge is meditation;
better than meditation is the renunciation
of the fruits of actions: peace

If, filled with egoism, thou thinkest, "I
will not fight," then thy resolve is vain;
nature will compel thee.

Abandon all duties and take refuge in Me
alone; I will liberate you from all sins;
do not grieve.
